<section id="Pt0.A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix 0.C </span>Class Distributions AEs</h2>

<div id="Pt0.A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we present the resulting class distributions of adversarial examples. In each Figure, the top row is the PGD starting from clean images, with <math id="Pt0.A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> as the target class. In the bottom row, we begin with backdoored images. Note that since the label for the backdoored image is always <math id="Pt0.A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, no images get misclassified as class <math id="Pt0.A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. We make a special case for the original label (before poisoning) and set it to <math id="Pt0.A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> class.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Pt0.A3.F11" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.10806v1/images/ae_boxplots/cifar100_vit_b_16_class_distribution_all_ratios_combined.png" id="Pt0.A3.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/152;" width="381" height="152" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span>Distributions of predicted classes for backdoored models on CIFAR-100. Starting from clean images (above) and poisoned images (below).</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Pt0.A3.F12" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.10806v1/images/ae_boxplots/tiny_vit_b_16_class_distribution_all_ratios_combined.png" id="Pt0.A3.F12.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/152;" width="381" height="152" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 12: </span>Distributions of predicted classes for backdoored models on Tiny-ImageNet. Starting from clean images (above) and poisoned images (below).</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Pt0.A3.F13" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.10806v1/images/ae_boxplots/cifar10_vit_b_16_class_distribution_all_ratios_combined.png" id="Pt0.A3.F13.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/152;" width="381" height="152" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 13: </span>Distributions of predicted classes for backdoored models on CIFAR-10. Starting from clean images (above) and poisoned images (below).</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
